WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.868
-Thank you, everybody.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.237
That was very nice.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.339
All right.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.208
I, uh...

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.409
I, uh -- As a comic,
I travel a lot.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:13.046
And I like to golf.
I'm a big golfer.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.448
And so, I will golf, sometimes,
when I go on the road.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:18.017
And I was golfing recently.
You get done,

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.952
you know,
you get very hot and sweaty.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.789
And I wanted to change shirts
before I drove back.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:26.192
So, I go to the trunk of my car,
in the parking lot.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.595
I take my shirt off.
I have no shirt on.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:32.665
And this old man walks up to me,
and goes, "Olivia?"

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.201
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.109
He was looking for
his elderly wife,

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:47.280
and saw me
with no shirt on,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.616
at a car that he
does not recognize.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.217
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.285
None of this is enough
to not make him see.

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:54.653
He's like, "Olivia?"

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:56.188
I was embarrassed.
I turned around.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.157
I covered up.
I was like, "What's that?"

00:00:58.157 --> 00:00:59.458
I go,
"What did you say?"

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.293
He was like, "All right, my bad.
Honest mistake."

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:03.630
And I was like, "God, that hurts
worse than saying 'Olivia.'"

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.832
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.403
I don't know who he offended
more -- me or Olivia.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.672
I think we could both have
a word with him.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.610
I'd love to meet her, though.
I'll tell you that.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.546
I'd love to see her, and be
like, "All right. I get it."

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.780
You know?
Like, just...

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.816
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.254
I'm married, as well.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:32.525
And my wife always tells me that
I don't like the way she talks.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.693
And it's not her voice.
I like the sound of her voice.

00:01:34.693 --> 00:01:36.028
That'd be a big problem,
I think,

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.064
if it was like, "It's your
voice. I just hate it."

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.532
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.100
To go to couple's therapy,
and be like,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.336
"Can you hear it?
Like, it's not...

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.238
You know,
it's not fun."

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:52.779
It's the information that she
chooses to tell me at times.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.180
We took a trip
to Ft. Lauderdale,

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.783
and her and our daughter
are flying from Nashville,

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.718
where we live.
And I was flying from Detroit.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:02.122
We're meeting at
Ft. Lauderdale's airport.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.922
I have to find them
when they land.

00:02:03.922 --> 00:02:05.758
So, I called her,
'cause I was about to take off,

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.226
and I was like, "All right.
What time do you guys leave?"

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.327
And she goes, "Noon."

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.062
It's 11:30,
and they're still at home.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:12.098
I was like, "Laura,
I don't know if you even know

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.266
what an airport is."

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:16.936
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.138
I mean, if that plane
was in our driveway,

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.239
I don't think
you could make it.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.542
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:25.611
She said, "That's what time
we leave for the airport.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:26.945
Our flight's
not till 1:30."

00:02:26.945 --> 00:02:29.048
And I was like,
"All right. Okay.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.217
So, what -- Like, what do
you think I wanted to know

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.318
when I asked that?"

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:36.489
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.457
I mean...

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:42.127
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:43.229
"Is that what you thought

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.397
the best information
you could give me,

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.633
was a time that means nothing
to nobody?"

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:47.766
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.766 --> 00:02:49.068
"What time did you
go to bed last night?

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.737
Just tell me that,
and I'll just look up

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.771
all the planes
that land in Florida,

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.941
and I'll guess which one
I think you're on."

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.208
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:57.810
She said,
"I'm sorry I don't talk

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.845
the way you want
me to talk."

00:02:58.845 --> 00:02:59.879
I'm like,
"I want you to talk

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.147
like a regular person,
all right?

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.683
Just, like you've been around
people, you know?"

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:07.053
We didn't talk in Florida.
I'll tell you that.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.756
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.994
She...

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.262
She's good at
not talking to me.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.797
She can go a long time.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.999
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.700
She gives me
the silent treatment.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.969
The silent treatment is --
It's very common.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:25.404
Everybody knows
what it is.

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:26.806
I think you're born
just knowing it.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.241
I don't think
you're taught it.

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:31.044
You know, it's not like my mom
did it, and her mom did it.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.146
It's an instinct
that is in us.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.747
And what made me
think of that is,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.150
I rewatched the movie
"Sixth Sense."

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.419
I'm not -- Look, I'm not trying
to do a "Six Sense" joke.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.121
This is a
20-year-old movie.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.689
I also have to spoil it
for you.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.058
But it's 20 years old,
so if you don't know by now,

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.061
then I don't --
you know, I don't know.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.194
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:51.497
There's other movies.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.666
And don't be like, "We were
gonna watch it tonight."

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.905
"We were gonna swing by
Blockbuster on the way home."

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.941
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:05.011
So, he's -- You know,
he's dead the whole time.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.379
And I mean,
if you haven't seen it,

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.281
that's a pretty big
part of it.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:11.184
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.586
If you have,
think about when we saw

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.788
this movie for the first time,
none of us knew he was dead.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.558
That was the biggest surprise
we've ever seen in a movie.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.393
We just thought his wife
wasn't talking to him

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.794
for, like, a year.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:26.365
That made more sense to us
than him possibly being dead.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:29.835
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.538
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.474
And they -- Like,
and they don't hide his death.

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.076
A guy shoots him
with a gun.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.111
The movie starts
with him dying.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.013
And we watched it for two hours,
just like,

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.448
"I know what this guy's
going through, you know?

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.918
This is a movie about marriage,
and how hard marriage is."

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.620
All right.
Thank you guys very much.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.854
I appreciate it.

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:50.956
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:58.998 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:01.267 line:0%
-Nate Bargatze, everybody.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.334 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.003 line:0%
Holy moly.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.338 line:0%
His stand-up special

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:08.041 line:0%
is available to stream now
on Netflix.

